<p>You can display the preview screen to check before printing. You can 
 also change some of the settings on the preview screen.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if you have already 
 installed Ridoc Desk Navigator, Ridoc Desk Navigator Lt, or Ridoc IO Navi. 
 For details about the settings, see the Help files for Ridoc Desk Navigator, 
 Ridoc Desk Navigator Lt, or Ridoc IO Navi.</p></li>
<li><p>Displaying the preview screen with this function 
 may take longer than normal printing. Using this function may also cause 
 your computer to run slowly.</p></li>
<li><p>This function may not be available in a "Point 
 and Print" environment.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Display Preview 
 and Print Screen</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the 
 printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>The preview screen appears.</p></li>
<li><p>Check the preview screen. Change settings as necessary.<br/>
 For details about preview screen settings, see the Help files for Ridoc 
 Desk Navigator, Ridoc Desk Navigator Lt, or Ridoc IO Navi.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">Print</span> to close 
 the preview screen.</p></li>
</ol>
